body:
Quick pass: good. Head `a728767` merges cleanly with `main`. On this head:
- the quick gate is green (394 steps, 0 failed), and clippy of `camcraft-app` and `camcraft-ui` is clean;
- the example catalog suites are green (`example_catalog` 50, `example_catalog_adaptive` 1, `example_catalog_edge_work` 1);
- the light lane is green (4 steps, 0 failed).

An independent pre-review found no blocking points. It confirms the outline rule. A converted holder compares its outline with the library body through `tool_body::checked_profile`, which is the profile the collision laws read, at every band edge. Identical gives "same". Wider at no height narrower gives "different", with the change listed. Narrower at any height gives "no match", and the convert refuses it by name. A test posts each row kind before and after the convert and checks that the program is the same.

This PR can change the holder body and shank length that the collision checks read (see the Safety floor section of the body), so the maintainer may want to merge it. I flag it ready for review.

@sn3ro, a UI/UX review from you is welcome on this PR (the "Convert to components…" preview in the tool list). A contributor's pre-check comment is fine; it is not a condition for the merge.
